o get dollars.**\n- **System C**: Decimal dollars as written. `386.54` is $386.54. No conversion needed.\n\nSo System B is the outlier—it's the only one in a different unit.\n\n**Dates:**\n\n- **System A**: ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD`. `2026-01-03` means January 3rd. Parse as-is.\n- **System B**: ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD`. `2026-01-07` means January 7th. Parse as-is.\n- **System C**: DD/MM/YYYY format. `02/01/2026` means the 2nd of the 1st month (January 2nd), not February 1st. **Must parse as DD/MM/YYYY, not YYYY-MM-DD.**\n\nSo System C is the outlier on dates—if you parse it as YYYY-MM-DD, `02/01/2026` would silently become February 1st when it should be January 2nd.\n\nThe reader for each system is the only place that knows its own date format and amount scaling, and that's by design—the reader hands raw strings to whoever builds records, and the caller converts them knowing which system it's dealing with.", "ttft_ms": 3675, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 7748, "uuid": "9e0379b7-5a0c-4a07-9cfc-e9fd03a57982", "ttft_stream_ms": 887, "time_to_request_ms": 85, "first_content_frame_ms": 1114, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 9.1, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--resume", "7898f056-59ba-46b5-a154-be964d81c23f"]}
