rmalized CSV\n- Reads multiple export files from systems A, B, or C in any order\n- Converts raw data to Record objects with proper type handling:\n  - **System A**: ISO dates (YYYY-MM-DD), decimal dollars\n  - **System B**: ISO dates (YYYY-MM-DD), integer cents (converted to dollars)\n  - **System C**: DD/MM/YYYY dates, decimal dollars\n- Normalizes records (strips whitespace, uppercases codes, collapses description whitespace)\n- Outputs to `out/records.csv` by default (customizable with `--out`)\n- Summary: `wrote=<count> to <path>`\n\n### 2. **`report`** — Totals by account or month\n- Reads normalized records file\n- Two modes with `--by`:\n  - `account`: Lists totals per account code, sorted ascending\n  - `month`: Lists totals per month (YYYY-MM), sorted chronologically\n- **Semicolon-delimited** columns (not commas, per HANDOVER spec update)\n- Refunds **included by default** in totals\n- Amounts formatted per `settings.decimals` with half-to-even rounding\n\n### 3. **`reconcile`** — Find system disagreements\n- Groups by account code, month, and source system\n- Reports account/month combinations where ≥2 systems posted with spread > tolerance\n- Format: `MISMATCH 4200 2026-02 spread=57.75 A=455.00 B=512.75 C=-`\n- Systems with no data shown as `-`\n- Ends with: `mismatches=<n>`\n\n### 4. **`validate`** — Reject malformed rows\n- Checks files without writing\n- Rejects rows with:\n  - Mismatched field counts\n  - Unparseable dates\n  - Unparseable amounts\n  - Account codes not matching regex pattern\n- One WARNING log per rejected row\n- Summary: `checked=<rows> rejected=<rows>`\n- Exit code: 0 (all pass) or 2 (any rejected)\n\n### 5. **`--config PATH`** — Settings override\n- Global option before subcommand\n- Sets `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` environment variable\n- Works with all subcommands\n\nAll tests pass and implementations follow all house rules (no print in library code, full type annotations, Decimal amounts, datetime.date dates, project logger, etc.).", 